Q3 -- the 1D strand-path delocalization classes (D6), derived with NUN's own D1/D2 method (bilinear smearing; tight-binding band with finite-size remainder), exponents BEFORE comparison:
   chord      ell ~ A^(1/3)    : smearing exponent +0.00 (fixed);  band-remainder exponent -0.598 -> nearest lattice -0.667 (OFF lattice); |exp - (-1/2)| = 0.10 (no loophole)
   surface walk ell ~ A^(2/3)  : smearing exponent +0.00 (fixed);  band-remainder exponent -1.314 -> nearest lattice -1.000 (OFF lattice); |exp - (-1/2)| = 0.81 (no loophole)
   space-filling ell ~ A       : smearing exponent +0.00 (fixed);  band-remainder exponent -1.995 -> nearest lattice -1.000 (OFF lattice); |exp - (-1/2)| = 1.49 (no loophole)
   Lattice {0, -1/3, -2/3, -1}: chord ON (-2/3); surface walk (-4/3) and space-filling (-2) OFF and far from -1/2. No path class produces root-extensivity.
